**How to implement.** `RecordExperiment` as a semantic message: a new experiment of the draft over the active setup, however many the setup already has (001 §P `RecordExperiment`; 001 §J 'Direct problem: several experiments over one setup, saved in the kit'; 001 §O 'Slot bar over the table (§J), with "Record experiment"'). The slot bar's button that sends it is step 280's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `ExpCommit`'s two halves (steps 152, 261 (8)(b), 272) become two private functions of the update, so no second copy of either is written (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'): the table recorded as the active setup (the recorded slots, `revisedWith` over `pinFor` when a setup is active or the template's name made free otherwise, `recordSetup` unless the setup is unchanged, then `kitSetups` and `activeSetupOpt`), and the recording of the experiments a commit appended (`recordExperiment`, step 261 (7)(b)). `ExpCommit` and `GenerateSetupGrid` (step 276, which records each appended experiment as `ExpCommit` records one) call them, every text and outcome unchanged. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `RecordExperiment`, with a one-line doc: a new experiment of the draft over the active setup. (3) Its arm is refused by the read-only guard of step 185, which every write message calls. Otherwise a draft that cannot be committed (`ExperimentCollection.canCommit`, `Experiments.fs:canCommit`: no element or no variable chosen) sets `kitStatus` to `Not recorded — choose the element and the variable to vary in the Experiments bay first.` and writes nothing, and with no capture (`model.draftCapture`, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1555`: no detector captures the table) `Not recorded — no detector captures this table.` and writes nothing. Else the table is recorded as the active setup through the first function, whose error keeps the model with `ExpCommit`'s `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`; then the collection takes the capture (`Experiments.chooseMeasurement`) and `Experiments.commitOverSetups [ setup.reference ]` (step 275), which appends the draft as a new experiment over that one reference whether or not the draft edits one and leaves the draft editing nothing, and the appended experiment is recorded through the second function, whose error keeps the collection with the same text. On success `kitStatus` is `Recorded <the experiment's id> over <setup.reference.describe>.` (`Recorded E2 over 'Bench' revision 1.`). So the direct problem is any number of experiments over one setup, each its own `<id>.experiment-json`, and a table changed since its setup was recorded is recorded first, as a commit records it. `ExpCommit` keeps editing the experiment its draft edits; `RecordExperiment` never edits one. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 260-264), over its folder kit: `RecordExperiment appends a new experiment over the active setup each time, so one setup holds several experiments`: with a linear polarizer added, `SetSetupName (ControlCaption "Bench")` and `CreateSetup`, the polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`), then `RecordExperiment`, the range's maximum changed (`ExpSetRangeMax`) and `RecordExperiment` again: the folder holds `E1.experiment-json` and `E2.experiment-json`, both referencing `'Bench' revision 1`, `E1` with the first range and `E2` with the changed one; the bytes of `Bench.setup-json` are those `CreateSetup` wrote; `kitStatus` is `Recorded E2 over 'Bench' revision 1.`; and the draft edits nothing. `RecordExperiment over a draft that edits an experiment appends another and leaves the edited one as it was`: after `E1` is recorded, `ExpEdit E1`, the range's maximum changed and `RecordExperiment` append `E2` with the changed range, and the bytes of `E1.experiment-json` are unchanged. `RecordExperiment records the table as ExpCommit does: a first setup for a table that is no setup yet, and the next revision over one an experiment references`: on a table that is no setup yet, with the polarizer chosen, `RecordExperiment` writes `Setup 1.setup-json` and `E1` over `'Setup 1' revision 1` and makes `Setup 1` active; the polarizer turned (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 30.0)`, it being selected) and `RecordExperiment` again give `Setup 1` revision 2 with revision 1 in its history and `E2` over revision 2, `E1` still referencing revision 1. `RecordExperiment without a chosen element and variable is told and writes nothing`: after `ExpNew`, with nothing chosen, `RecordExperiment` sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not recorded` and the folder holds no experiment file. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 185, 262, 273): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `RecordExperiment`, with the same assertions. Every `ExpCommit` and `GenerateSetupGrid` fact passes unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After `RecordExperiment` lands, it MUST record the table as `ExpCommit` records it and append a new experiment of the draft over the active setup each time, never editing the draft's own, and refuse a draft that cannot be committed and a read-only kit with nothing written, `ExpCommit` and `GenerateSetupGrid` sharing its two halves unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `RecordExperiment appends a new experiment over the active setup each time, so one setup holds several experiments`, `RecordExperiment over a draft that edits an experiment appends another and leaves the edited one as it was`, `RecordExperiment records the table as ExpCommit does: a first setup for a table that is no setup yet, and the next revision over one an experiment references` and `RecordExperiment without a chosen element and variable is told and writes nothing` and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.
